---
description: Choose ME* widgets from material3_expressive when writing Flutter UI. Use when building screens, replacing Material widgets, or deciding which library control to use.
globs: "**/*.dart"
alwaysApply: false
---

When writing Flutter UI in this repo (or any app that depends on
`material3_expressive`), **load and follow**
`.cursor/skills/material3-expressive/SKILL.md`.

- Public widgets use the **`ME` prefix**, never `M3E`.
- Map intent → widget from the skill. If unsure, open
  `.cursor/skills/material3-expressive/catalog.md`.
- Copy constructors from
  `.cursor/skills/material3-expressive/constructors.md` or the source under
  `lib/src/`. Do not invent APIs and do not copy pub.dev
  `material_3_expressive`.
- Wrap the app with `METheme`. `MEAppBar` is a **sliver**. Prefer `MEMenu`
  over `PopupMenuButton`. Do not use deprecated `ExpressiveButton`.
